#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:1
msgid "Tile Libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:3
msgid ""
"A Tile kernel operates on whole tiles without naming individual threads. A "
"SIMT function operates on elements from individual threads or warps. A "
"**tile library** connects the two: it packages Rust device functions so the "
"Tile compiler can call them from inside a Tile kernel and link them into a "
"single `cubin`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:9
msgid "**Annotate in Rust:** Mark device functions with `#[tile_export]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:10
msgid ""
"**Package the library:** Run `cargo oxide tilelib` to emit compiled device "
"code and Tile IR metadata, packaged into a `.tilelib` archive by `tileiras` "
"(CUDA 13.5+)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:13
msgid ""
"**Call from a Tile kernel:** Invoke the exported function from Tile C++ or "
"cuTile Python, with [cutile-rs](https://nvidia.github.io/cuda-rust/cutile/) "
"caller support to follow."
msgstr ""

