#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:266
msgid "How to read the two sections:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:268
msgid ""
"**Interface (`preview$func extern`):** Lists each function as the Tile "
"kernel sees it, taking `tile<128xf32>` inputs and returning all `inout` and "
"`out` tiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:271
msgid ""
"**Implementation (`preview$extern_impl`):** Maps each C symbol "
"(`@relu_impl`) to the per-invocation `fragment` it receives. `mem_layout` is "
"`():()` for a by-value scalar and `(1):(1)` for a pointer to 1 element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:274
msgid ""
"**Fragment map (`fragmap`):** Maps `(invocations, participants, footprint)` "
"across the tile:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:276
msgid ""
"`(128, 1, 1):(1, 0, 0)` runs **128 independent thread invocations** of 1 "
"element each (`sync = \"none\"`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:278
msgid ""
"`(4, 32, 1):(32, 1, 0)` runs **4 warp invocations of 32 lanes** each (`sync "
"= \"warp\"`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:283
msgid "Building a Provider Library (`--provider`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:289
msgid ""
"Provider tile library flow. The `.tilelib` embeds a shared library that "
"`tileiras` loads while compiling a Tile kernel, generating and compiling "
"size-specific wrapper symbols on demand from a single Rust function body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:294
msgid ""
"When an export omits `tile_shape`, its declaration is parametric in the tile "
"size: `@relu_any<[N: index]>(tile<[N]xf32>)`. Because compiled device "
"functions in Tile IR are never generic, calling `relu_any` at sizes 128 and "
"256 requires two distinct symbols (`relu_any_impl__N128` and "
"`relu_any_impl__N256`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:299
msgid ""
"Instead of prebuilding symbols for every possible size, pass `--provider` to "
"package a linkage provider shared library:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:302
msgid "cargo oxide tilelib tilelib_relu --arch sm_120 --provider\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:306
msgid "How provider mode works:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:308
msgid ""
"**Embed NVVM IR at build time:** `cargo oxide tilelib --provider` embeds "
"your crate's NVVM IR (`.ll`) and export metadata into a generated `cdylib` "
"(`lib<crate>_provider.so`), then combines the interface bytecode and `.so` "
"into `<crate>.tilelib`. Both parametric and fixed-size exports are included."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:312
msgid ""
"**Load during Tile compilation:** When `tileiras` compiles a Tile kernel "
"against the library, it loads the `.tilelib` shared object via `dlopen`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:314
msgid ""
"**Resolve each call site:** For every foreign call in the kernel (such as "
"`relu_any<128>` and `relu_any<256>`), `tileiras` queries the provider for "
"matching implementations and assigns a concrete symbol per tile size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:317
msgid ""
"**Compile requested sizes on demand:** `tileiras` requests the device code "
"once for all chosen symbols. The provider appends a thin wrapper per symbol "
"that tail-calls your Rust function, compiles the module to LTOIR with "
"`libNVVM`, and hands it back to `tileiras` for final linking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:322
msgid ""
"Set `OXIDE_TILE_PROVIDER_LOG=1` when compiling a Tile kernel to print every "
"query from `tileiras` and every symbol compiled by the provider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:327
msgid "Calling from a Tile Kernel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:329
msgid "From Tile C++"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:331
msgid ""
"With CUDA 13.5 or newer, `nvcc` supports `--enable-tile` and `--tile-preview "
"simt`. Declare exported functions with `__experimental_foreign_decl__`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:335
msgid ""
"namespace ct = cuda::tiles;\n"
"using tile_f32 = ct::tile<float, ct::shape<128>>;\n"
"\n"
"// Fixed-size export: @relu(tile<128xf32> in, tile<128xf32> out) -> "
"tile<128xf32>\n"
"__experimental_foreign_decl__ __experimental_foreign_name__(\"relu\")\n"
"    tile_f32 relu(tile_f32 x, [[cutile::experimental_inout]] tile_f32 "
"relu_out);\n"
"\n"
"[[cutile::hint(0, num_worker_warps_per_cta = 4)]] __tile_global__ void "
"kernel(float* x, float* y) {\n"
"    auto xs = ct::partition_view { ct::tensor_span { x, ct::shape<128> {} }, "
"ct::shape<128> {} };\n"
"    auto ys = ct::partition_view { ct::tensor_span { y, ct::shape<128> {} }, "
"ct::shape<128> {} };\n"
"    ys.store(relu(xs.load(0), ys.load(0)), 0);\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:350
msgid "Compile and run with `nvcc`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:352
msgid ""
"nvcc --enable-tile --tile-preview simt -Xtileiras=-l=tilelib_relu.tilelib "
"\\\n"
"     -std=c++20 -arch=sm_120 -o tile_caller cpp/tile_caller.cu\n"
"./tile_caller\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:358
msgid ""
"For parametric exports in a `--provider` library, declare a C++ function "
"template parameterized by the tile extent `N` (see `cpp/"
"tile_caller_parametric.cu`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:362
msgid ""
"template <size_t N>\n"
"__experimental_foreign_decl__ __experimental_foreign_name__(\"relu_any\")\n"
"    ct::tile<float, ct::shape<N>> relu_any(\n"
"        ct::tile<float, ct::shape<N>> x,\n"
"        [[cutile::experimental_inout]] ct::tile<float, ct::shape<N>> "
"relu_any_out);\n"
"\n"
"// Instantiates relu_any_impl__N128 and relu_any_impl__N256 on demand:\n"
"relu128.store(relu_any<128>(view<128>(ramp128).load(0), relu128.load(0)), "
"0);\n"
"relu256.store(relu_any<256>(view<256>(ramp256).load(0), relu256.load(0)), "
"0);\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:374
msgid "Key points for Tile C++ callers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:376
msgid ""
"**Input vs. output attributes:** Read-only parameters take no attribute; "
"`inout` and `out` parameters take `[[cutile::experimental_inout]]` and are "
"returned as the call result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:379
msgid ""
"**Use the declaration name:** Pass `\"relu\"` (not `\"relu_impl\"`) to "
"`__experimental_foreign_name__`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:381
msgid ""
"**Matched toolchain:** Because `nvcc` and `tileiras` come from the same CUDA "
"toolkit, their Tile IR bytecode versions always match."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:384
msgid "From cuTile Python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:386
msgid ""
"In cuTile Python, load the `.tilelib` at module scope and invoke exports "
"with `cuda.tile_preview.foreign_call` (from `python/call_from_cutile.py`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:389
msgid ""
"import cuda.tile as ct\n"
"from cuda import tile_preview as tp\n"
"\n"
"TILE = 128\n"
"PROVIDER = tp.Tilelib(path=\"tilelib_relu.tilelib\", version=\"0.1.0\")\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def relu_tile(x, y):\n"
"    \"\"\"Run Rust `relu` over one 128-float tile per block.\"\"\"\n"
"    pid = ct.bid(0)\n"
"    tile = ct.load(x, index=(pid,), shape=(TILE,))\n"
"    result_slot = ct.zeros((TILE,), dtype=ct.float32)\n"
"    (out,) = tp.foreign_call(\n"
"        tilelibs=(PROVIDER,),\n"
"        symbol_name=\"relu\",\n"
"        constant_params=(),\n"
"        inputs=(tile, result_slot),\n"
"        output_types=((ct.float32, (TILE,)),),\n"
"    )\n"
"    ct.store(y, index=(pid,), tile=out)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:412
msgid "Key points for cuTile Python callers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:414
msgid "**Declaration name:** Pass `symbol_name=\"relu\"`, not `\"relu_impl\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:415
msgid ""
"**Pass a tile for every parameter:** `inputs` must supply a tile for every "
"declaration argument, including output slots (`result_slot = ct.zeros(...)`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:417
msgid ""
"**Specify `output_types`:** Provide one `(dtype, shape)` tuple per `inout` "
"or `out` parameter in declaration order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:419
msgid ""
"**Parametric exports:** When calling a `--provider` export without a fixed "
"`tile_shape`, pass the tile extent in `constant_params=(TILE,)` instead of "
"`()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:425
msgid "Execution Model and Current Limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:427
msgid "What Happens at the SIMT Boundary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:429
msgid ""
"The Tile compiler never passes an entire tile to a single Rust call. "
"Instead, it partitions each tile into per-invocation fragments in local "
"memory or registers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:432
msgid ""
"**Per-element (`sync = \"none\"`):** A 128-element tile with footprint 1 "
"runs 128 calls, each on one thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:434
msgid ""
"**Per-warp (`sync = \"warp\"`):** Each invocation is a full 32-lane hardware "
"warp. Every lane receives its own element(s), and warp collectives "
"(`cuda_device::warp`) are valid inside the function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:437
msgid ""
"**Private fragment pointers:** Reference parameters (`&T`, `&mut T`, `&[T; "
"F]`) point strictly to that invocation's own elements (`1` or `F` contiguous "
"values). Do not index past them, and never assume adjacent threads' "
"fragments are contiguous in memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:441
msgid ""
"**Registers only (no shared memory):** The Tile compiler owns shared-memory "
"allocation for the kernel. Do not declare `SharedArray` inside a "
"`#[tile_export]` function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:445
msgid "Current Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:447
msgid ""
"**Synchronization scopes:** `sync` supports `\"none\"` and `\"warp\"` only "
"(warpgroup and CTA scopes are not yet available)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:449
msgid ""
"**Tile rank and element types:** Only 1D tiles and `f16`, `f32`, `f64`, and "
"8/16/32/64-bit integer types are supported (`bf16` and 2D tiles are not yet "
"supported)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:452
msgid ""
"**No shared-memory scratch:** Exports cannot request a shared-memory scratch "
"buffer from the Tile compiler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:454
msgid ""
"**Workspace requirement for `--provider`:** Building a `--provider` library "
"currently requires running inside the `cuda-oxide` workspace so the "
"generated provider crate can reference `oxide-tile-provider` by path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:457
msgid ""
"**Caller front ends:** Tile C++ and cuTile Python can call tile libraries "
"today; `cutile-rs` caller support is planned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:460
msgid ""
"See [Supported Features](../appendix/supported-features.md) for the full "
"compiler feature matrix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:463
msgid "Verifying the ABI on CUDA 13.4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:465
msgid ""
"Even without the CUDA 13.5 `tileiras` assembler, you can test the generated "
"SIMT wrappers and ABI end-to-end on a GPU using the example's host harness:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:468
msgid "cargo oxide run tilelib_relu --emit-nvvm-ir --arch sm_120\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:472
msgid ""
"The host runner reads `tilelib_relu.tileexports.json`, generates a CUDA C++ "
"caller (`mock/caller.cu`) with the exact prototypes derived from the export "
"descriptions, links it with the Rust LTOIR via `nvJitLink`, and verifies all "
"5 exports on the GPU:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:477
msgid ""
"PASS relu: 128 elements through `relu_impl`, relu of a ramp from -4 to 4\n"
"PASS scale_in_place: 128 elements through `scale_in_place_impl`, the ramp "
"scaled in place by 0.5\n"
"PASS warp_sum: 128 elements through `warp_sum_impl`, 32-lane sums over "
"0..128, every lane holding its warp's total\n"
"PASS relu_any: 128 elements through `relu_any_impl`, relu of a ramp from -4 "
"to 4\n"
"PASS warp_sum_any: 128 elements through `warp_sum_any_impl`, 32-lane sums "
"over 0..128, every lane holding its warp's total\n"
"SUCCESS: 5/5 tile exports verified through the native ABI\n"
msgstr ""
